<h2 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-an-impromptu-visit-to-turkiye">An Impromptu Visit to Turkiye</h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">If you&rsquo;re in your late 40s like I am, and lucky enough to still have your parents, you might also be navigating the reality of them aging.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Longtime readers might remember that my dad lived with us here in the U.S. during Covid. But the language barrier made daily life tough for him, and eventually, he decided to return home to Turkiye.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Physically, he&rsquo;s still doing well. But over the last six months, a doctor&rsquo;s visit revealed that he&rsquo;s started showing early signs of dementia.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image aligncenter size-full"><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="893" data-pin-nopin="true" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/my-dad.jpg" alt="Photos from my trip to Turkiye." class="wp-image-81954" srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/my-dad.jpg 1200w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/my-dad-350x260.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/my-dad-768x572.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/my-dad-400x298.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/my-dad-150x112.jpg 150w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/my-dad.jpg"></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">As soon as I heard that, I booked a ticket. I needed to see him in person, to get a better sense of what was going on and what needed to be done.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">We&rsquo;re lucky that he has a support system there, but as an only child, I want to stay as close and involved as I can.&nbsp;</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">So this trip turned into a bit of a father-daughter getaway. We went to Marmaris, a small town on the Mediterranean coast, to visit my cousin and her family. It ended up being the most peaceful and much-needed four days: swimming in the sea, sharing meals, and soaking up that comforting presence of family.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image aligncenter size-full"><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="893" data-pin-nopin="true" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/family-marmaris.jpg" alt="Postcards from my trip to Turkiye." class="wp-image-81955" srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/family-marmaris.jpg 1200w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/family-marmaris-350x260.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/family-marmaris-768x572.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/family-marmaris-400x298.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/family-marmaris-150x112.jpg 150w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/family-marmaris.jpg"></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">I found myself wanting to stop time. Watching my dad and my aging aunts and uncles, I felt the weight and beauty of it all. Many of them are now facing health challenges, but I also saw their strength and wisdom with fresh eyes. I think I&rsquo;m at a point in life where I&rsquo;m finally able to truly appreciate it.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">I did my best to be present and soak up every conversation and quiet moment. It&rsquo;s hard to describe, but the emotions were mixed. There was some sadness, some clarity, and a deeper understanding of where we all are in life.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The rest of my time there was focused on making sure my dad is set up with the right support, has what he needs, and is surrounded by people who care about him.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image aligncenter size-full"><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="893" data-pin-nopin="true" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/yasemin.jpg" alt="An image with my friend Yasemin and food." class="wp-image-81956" srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/yasemin.jpg 1200w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/yasemin-350x260.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/yasemin-768x572.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/yasemin-400x298.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/yasemin-150x112.jpg 150w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/yasemin.jpg"></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Before heading back, I spent one last evening in Istanbul catching up with two of my childhood best friends. We laughed, we reminisced, and shared a beautiful seafood dinner by the Bosphorus.&nbsp;</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The view, the conversation, and the food all came together in a way that made the night feel extra special. It was the perfect way to wrap up an emotional and unforgettable trip.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image aligncenter size-full"><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="893" data-pin-nopin="true" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/ahu.jpg" alt="An image with my friend Ahu and a cup of Turkish coffee." class="wp-image-81957" srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/ahu.jpg 1200w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/ahu-350x260.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/ahu-768x572.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/ahu-400x298.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/ahu-150x112.jpg 150w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/ahu.jpg"></figure>
