<h2 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-in-the-now">In The Now</h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Since it&rsquo;s been a while, I&rsquo;m switching things up a bit with these life updates. Instead of listing what&rsquo;s working and what&rsquo;s not, I thought I&rsquo;d simply share a few things that are current in my world right now.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">No particular order. Just real life, as it is.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Some of these are affiliate links, which means if you make a purchase by clicking on a link, I may receive a commission at no cost to you.</p>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-currently-reading-outlive-by-dr-peter-attia">Currently Reading: <a href="https://amzn.to/4nvyidl" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener nofollow"><em>Outlive</em> by Dr. Peter Attia</a>:</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Spending time with my dad made a few things click for me. I want to age well and be more intentional about my health. This book has been eye-opening. It talks about how many of the diseases we see later in life actually begin much earlier, and how there are things we can do now to slow them down&mdash;or even prevent them altogether. It&rsquo;s written in a way that&rsquo;s easy to follow, and even though I&rsquo;m only halfway through its 400+ pages, I&rsquo;ve already learned so much.</p>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-learning-from-sarah-snow"><strong>Learning from: Sarah Snow</strong></h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">I&rsquo;ve been following <a href="https://www.instagram.com/iamsarahsnow/" rel="nofollow">Sarah on Instagram</a> for a while and have always loved her calm storytelling and beautiful filmmaking.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">So when she announced her new program, Viral You, I signed up right away. I&rsquo;ve been going through the lessons and doing the homework whenever I have time outside of work, and let me just say&mdash;there&rsquo;s been a lot of soul searching.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">I feel a strong pull to tell my story through food, but if I&rsquo;m being honest, I don&rsquo;t fully know how to do that yet. This course has been incredibly helpful. It&rsquo;s pushing me out of my comfort zone in the best way. I haven&rsquo;t shared anything publicly yet, and I don&rsquo;t feel quite ready for that switch, but I&rsquo;m working on it.</p>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-shopping-more-intentionally">Shopping (more intentionally)</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">One of the biggest lessons from our recent move is how much stuff we&rsquo;ve collected over the years. So much of it we didn&rsquo;t really need. Moving reminded me that I want to be more thoughtful with what I bring into our home moving forward.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Here are a few things I&rsquo;ve bought recently that have either made my life better or taught me a lesson or two. Some I absolutely love and would recommend without hesitation, and others didn&rsquo;t quite work out the way I&rsquo;d hoped. Thought I&rsquo;d share both.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image aligncenter size-full"><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="1800" data-pin-nopin="true" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/IMG_4380.jpg" alt="Photos of Aysegul wearing a black dress in the kitchen." class="wp-image-81958" srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/IMG_4380.jpg 1200w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/IMG_4380-350x525.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/IMG_4380-768x1152.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/IMG_4380-1024x1536.jpg 1024w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/IMG_4380-400x600.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/IMG_4380-150x225.jpg 150w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/IMG_4380.jpg"></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong><a href="https://rstyle.me/+iQZpwQzj1ZnVh4D72aIFLw" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener nofollow">The Black Dress from Madewell</a><br></strong>I&rsquo;ve always loved a good black dress, and this one has become a favorite of mine. It&rsquo;s flattering, comfortable, and has enough weight that it isn&rsquo;t see-through like so many linen dresses are these days. I wore it on repeat while I was in Turkiye. It&rsquo;s great for travel and works for so many occasions.</p>



