<h2 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-i-leave-you-with-this"><strong>I Leave You With This</strong></h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Between going back home and learning from Sarah, I&rsquo;ve found myself doing a lot of soul searching. What you see on this website and social media is just one part of me. It&rsquo;s the part that&rsquo;s my job.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image aligncenter size-full"><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="893" data-pin-nopin="true" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/breakfast.jpg" alt="Aysegul in a hamack and breakfast." class="wp-image-81975" srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/breakfast.jpg 1200w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/breakfast-350x260.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/breakfast-768x572.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/breakfast-400x298.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/breakfast-150x112.jpg 150w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/breakfast.jpg"></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Looking back, now twelve years into writing this blog, I can see that there&rsquo;s been a fair bit of pretending along the way. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Not because I wanted to be someone else, but because I grew up with a very traditional, conservative mom who taught me to be a lady. Speak only when it truly matters. Don&rsquo;t share too much. Don&rsquo;t show all your cards.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">There&rsquo;s a quote Sarah shared in her class that I haven&rsquo;t been able to stop thinking about:</p>



<blockquote class="wp-block-quote is-layout-flow wp-block-quote-is-layout-flow">
<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>The discomfort of being honest is so much easier than the exhaustion of pretending.</strong></p>
</blockquote>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">At this point in my life, I&rsquo;m searching for ways to be more honest and more vulnerable. To show up fully as myself, even if it feels uncomfortable at times. Because after all these years of putting myself out there, I&rsquo;ve realized it takes more energy to hold parts of myself back than to just be real with you.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">I know this won&rsquo;t happen overnight, but I&rsquo;m going to try. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">And if you&rsquo;re still here, still reading, then you&rsquo;ve got a front-row seat as I figure it out.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Until next month,</p>



